      "text": "To compute the **average speed** for the entire trip, we use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Average Speed} = \\frac{\\text{Total Distance}}{\\text{Total Time}}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Total Distance\n\n- First part: 180 km  \n- Second part: 90 km  \n\n$$\n\\text{Total Distance} = 180 + 90 = 270 \\text{ km}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Total Time\n\n- First part: 2.5 hours  \n- Second part: 1.5 hours  \n\n$$\n\\text{Total Time} = 2.5 + 1.5 = 4.0 \\text{ hours}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Average Speed\n\n$$\n\\text{Average Speed} = \\frac{270 \\text{ km}}{4.0 \\text{ h}} = 67.5 \\text{ km/h}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{67.5} \\text{ km/h}\n$$",
